  'draft', 'advanced',
  'A 45-year-old man of Afro-Caribbean descent presents with progressive breathlessness and bilateral ankle swelling. Echocardiography reveals a restrictive filling pattern with preserved ejection fraction, biatrial enlargement, and increased ventricular wall thickness with a granular/sparkling appearance. ECG shows low voltage in the limb leads despite the increased wall thickness on echo. Renal function shows proteinuria on urinalysis.',
  'Which investigation is most likely to confirm the underlying diagnosis?',
  array['cardiac amyloidosis','restrictive cardiomyopathy','diagnostic workup']
),
('d0000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000018', 'mrcp2', '3c307550-8d07-4fbf-b41d-51e666130165',
  'draft', 'advanced',
  'A 59-year-old woman with HFrEF (LVEF 32%) secondary to non-ischaemic dilated cardiomyopathy has been on optimal guideline-directed medical therapy for 6 months (sacubitril-valsartan, bisoprolol, spironolactone, dapagliflozin, all at target or maximally tolerated doses). Repeat echocardiogram shows LVEF now 34%. She remains NYHA class II. There is no history of sustained ventricular arrhythmia.',
  'What is the most appropriate approach regarding primary prevention ICD implantation?',
  array['primary prevention ICD','non-ischaemic cardiomyopathy','reassessment after GDMT']
),
('d0000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000019', 'mrcp2', 'b82172f5-bfe3-485e-a22f-2f58afbd1396',
  'draft', 'advanced',
  'A 44-year-old woman is investigated for resistant hypertension (BP 168/102 mmHg despite amlodipine, ramipril and indapamide at maximal tolerated doses, with confirmed adherence). She reports muscle cramps and bloods show potassium 3.1 mmol/L with mild metabolic alkalosis. Plasma aldosterone is markedly elevated with a suppressed plasma renin, giving a high aldosterone-to-renin ratio. CT adrenal imaging shows a 1.5cm left adrenal nodule with a normal-appearing right adrenal gland.',
  'What is the most appropriate next investigation before deciding on definitive management?',
  array['primary hyperaldosteronism','adrenal vein sampling','resistant hypertension']
),
