  'draft', 'advanced',
  'A 68-year-old man with a background of type 2 diabetes and chronic kidney disease (eGFR 38 mL/min/1.73m2, ACR 45 mg/mmol) has hypertension poorly controlled on maximal-dose ramipril and amlodipine (BP 156/94 mmHg). He is already on a maximally tolerated SGLT2 inhibitor for renal protection. Potassium is 4.6 mmol/L.',
  'What is the most appropriate next step to further reduce his blood pressure?',
  array['resistant hypertension','chronic kidney disease','add-on antihypertensive']
),
('d0000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000021', 'mrcp2', 'b82172f5-bfe3-485e-a22f-2f58afbd1396',
  'draft', 'advanced',
