  'draft', 'advanced',
  'A 41-year-old woman who injects drugs presents with fever and pleuritic chest pain. Blood cultures grow Staphylococcus aureus. Transthoracic echocardiogram shows a large mobile vegetation on the tricuspid valve. CT chest reveals multiple bilateral peripheral nodular opacities, some cavitating, consistent with septic pulmonary emboli. She has no signs of right heart failure and is haemodynamically stable.',
