  'draft', 'advanced',
  'A 72-year-old man is being treated for native aortic valve endocarditis due to penicillin-susceptible Streptococcus mitis with a 4-week course of IV benzylpenicillin. On day 12 of treatment, he develops a witnessed episode of expressive dysphasia lasting 20 minutes with full recovery. CT head shows a small acute infarct in the left MCA territory with no haemorrhage. He remains haemodynamically stable with no new murmur and no evidence of heart failure.',
  'What is the most appropriate next step regarding his endocarditis management?',
  array['embolic stroke in endocarditis','timing of surgery','anticoagulation considerations']
