  'draft', 'core',
  'A 27-year-old man presents 10 days after an upper respiratory tract viral illness with sharp central chest pain, worse lying flat and relieved sitting forward, associated with a low-grade fever. ECG shows widespread concave ST elevation and PR depression. Troponin is mildly elevated. Echocardiography shows a small pericardial effusion with normal biventricular function.',
  'What is the most appropriate first-line pharmacological management?',
  array['acute pericarditis','first-line therapy','myopericarditis']
),
