  'draft', 'advanced',
  'A 66-year-old woman is admitted with breathlessness and hypotension (BP 84/60 mmHg) three days after an anterior STEMI treated with primary PCI. She has a raised JVP with a prominent x descent and a pulsus paradoxus of 18 mmHg. Bedside echocardiography shows a large circumferential pericardial effusion with diastolic collapse of the right ventricle. Heart rate is 118 bpm.',
  'What is the most appropriate immediate management?',
  array['cardiac tamponade','post-MI pericardial effusion','urgent pericardiocentesis']
),
