  'draft', 'core',
  'A 52-year-old man with end-stage renal disease on haemodialysis presents with progressive breathlessness and is found to have a large pericardial effusion on echocardiography without overt tamponade features currently, though early signs of right atrial diastolic collapse are noted. He has missed several recent dialysis sessions.',
  'What is the most appropriate initial management approach?',
  array['uraemic pericarditis','dialysis-related effusion','intensified dialysis']
),
