  'draft', 'advanced',
  'An 82-year-old man with severe symptomatic aortic stenosis (mean gradient 52 mmHg, aortic valve area 0.7cm2, NYHA class III) is assessed by the heart team. He has significant frailty, chronic kidney disease (eGFR 35 mL/min/1.73m2), and a EuroSCORE II suggesting high surgical risk. CT assessment confirms suitable femoral access and favourable annular anatomy for a transcatheter approach.',
  'What is the most appropriate management approach?',
  array['severe aortic stenosis','TAVI','heart team decision-making']
),
