  'draft', 'advanced',
  'A 71-year-old woman is found to have a secundum atrial septal defect on echocardiography performed for investigation of exertional breathlessness. There is evidence of right ventricular dilatation and mild right ventricular systolic dysfunction, with a calculated pulmonary-to-systemic flow ratio (Qp:Qs) of 2.2:1. Right heart catheterisation shows a pulmonary vascular resistance of 2.5 Wood units, well below the threshold associated with irreversible pulmonary vascular disease.',
